  "body_html": "<h2>Problem</h2>\n<p>I read in English and Vietnamese, mostly paper books. I wanted to know how much I really read, at what pace, and when I will finish the current book. A habit tracker only works if logging is quick, so the first rule was that recording a session should take seconds. The second was that the dashboard could be public while the raw diary stays private.</p>\n<p>The data is my own: one row per book and one per reading session, with start and end time and pages. Until my history is imported, the dashboard runs on a seeded demo history of 15 books and 180 sessions over 182 days, labelled as demo data<sup class=\"cite\"><a href=\"#sources\" title=\"Source: vault note reading-tracker\">[src]</a></sup>.</p>\n<h2>Approach</h2>\n<figure class=\"fig\"><div class=\"fig-title\">From a button press to a public dashboard, with the private data kept at home</div><div class=\"flow\"><div class=\"stage\" style=\"flex-grow:1\"><div class=\"stage-label\">1 · Capture</div><div class=\"stage-boxes\"><div class=\"box\"><div class=\"box-label\">Private tracker</div><div class=\"box-detail\">Start and Stop buttons, prefilled with the last page</div><ul class=\"box-specs\"><li>Streamlit, localhost only</li><li>Live timer</li><li>Past sessions entered by hand</li><li>Add, finish or abandon a book</li></ul><div class=\"box-metrics\"><span class=\"chip\"><b>Coverage</b> 96.71%</span></div></div></div><div class=\"stage-out\">→ one reading session</div></div><div class=\"arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div><div class=\"stage\" style=\"flex-grow:1\"><div class=\"stage-label\">2 · Validate and store</div><div class=\"stage-boxes\"><div class=\"box\"><div class=\"box-label\">Rules, then SQLite</div><div class=\"box-detail\">Bad rows are refused before they are saved</div><ul class=\"box-specs\"><li>One active session at a time</li><li>No overlapping or future sessions</li><li>Positions within the book</li><li>ISO 8601 timestamps with UTC offset</li><li>Text in Unicode NFC</li></ul><div class=\"box-metrics\"><span class=\"chip\"><b>Tests</b> 109</span><span class=\"chip\"><b>Coverage</b> 100%</span></div></div></div><div class=\"stage-out\">→ books + sessions, raw events only</div></div><div class=\"arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div><div class=\"stage stage--parallel\" style=\"flex-grow:1.6\"><div class=\"stage-label\">3 · Publish</div><div class=\"stage-boxes\"><div class=\"box\"><div class=\"box-label\">Privacy export</div><div class=\"box-detail\">My real data, only what is safe to show</div><ul class=\"box-specs\"><li>Notes dropped</li><li>Start times floored to the hour</li><li>End times dropped, duration kept</li><li>Active sessions left out</li></ul><div class=\"box-metrics\"><span class=\"chip\"><b>Coverage</b> 94.12%</span></div></div><div class=\"box\"><div class=\"box-label\">Demo history</div><div class=\"box-detail\">Synthetic, so anyone can run the dashboard</div><ul class=\"box-specs\"><li>Seed 10, 182 days</li><li>15 books, 180 sessions</li><li>English and Vietnamese</li><li>Same validation as real data</li></ul><div class=\"box-metrics\"><span class=\"chip\"><b>Coverage</b> 99.02%</span></div></div></div><div class=\"stage-out\">→ public tables</div></div><div class=\"arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div><div class=\"stage stage--parallel\" style=\"flex-grow:1.6\"><div class=\"stage-label\">4 · Derive</div><div class=\"stage-boxes\"><div class=\"box\"><div class=\"box-label\">Reading features</div><div class=\"box-detail\">Pure pandas functions, nothing stored</div><ul class=\"box-specs\"><li>Duration, pages, pages per minute</li><li>Daily minutes, current and longest streak</li><li>Midnight sessions count for their start date</li><li>Audiobooks left out of page pace</li></ul><div class=\"box-metrics\"><span class=\"chip\"><b>Coverage</b> 100%</span></div></div><div class=\"box\"><div class=\"box-label\">Finish estimate</div><div class=\"box-detail\">Baseline: two plain ratios, nothing learned</div><ul class=\"box-specs\"><li>Pages left ÷ median pace ÷ minutes per day</li><li>Last 28 days of reading</li><li>Range from 25th and 75th percentile pace</li></ul><div class=\"box-metrics\"><span class=\"chip\"><b>Coverage</b> 95.12%</span></div></div></div><div class=\"stage-out\">→ pace, streaks, finish date</div></div><div class=\"arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div><div class=\"stage stage--out\" style=\"flex-grow:1\"><div class=\"stage-label\">5 · Show</div><div class=\"stage-boxes\"><div class=\"box\"><div class=\"box-label\">Dashboard</div><div class=\"box-detail\">Streamlit and Plotly</div><ul class=\"box-specs\"><li>Current book and finish range</li><li>Calendar heatmap and streaks</li><li>Weekly minutes against a goal</li><li>Pace by genre, format, language</li><li>Timeline of finished books</li></ul><div class=\"box-metrics\"><span class=\"chip\"><b>Coverage</b> 94.87%</span></div></div></div><div class=\"stage-out\">→ public dashboard</div></div></div><figcaption>Stages 1 and 2 run on my computer only. The dashboard reads either the privacy-safe export or the synthetic demo history, never the raw database. Coverage: the share of a module&#x27;s statements that the tests run.</figcaption></figure>\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Validate where the data is born.</strong> Only one session can be open. Sessions cannot overlap or end in the future, and page positions must sit inside the book. Bad rows never reach the analysis. These rules carry 109 of the 206 tests<sup class=\"cite\"><a href=\"#sources\" title=\"Source: vault note reading-tracker\">[src]</a></sup>.</li>\n<li><strong>Store events, derive the rest.</strong> SQLite holds only books and sessions. Pace, streaks and progress are computed in pandas each time, so fixing a rule changes every past number consistently.</li>\n<li><strong>Private by construction.</strong> The export drops notes and end times and floors start times to the hour. It keeps each session's duration, because rounding both ends would turn a 20:10 to 20:40 session into zero minutes<sup class=\"cite\"><a href=\"#sources\" title=\"Source: vault note reading-tracker\">[src]</a></sup>.</li>\n<li><strong>A baseline before a model.</strong> The finish date is two plain ratios: pages left over recent median pace, over recent minutes per day. The range comes from the slower and faster quartiles of pace, so anyone can check it by hand.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Result</h2>\n<figure class=\"fig\"><div class=\"fig-title\">The data rules are fully tested; the Windows launcher is the gap</div><div class=\"dotplot\"><div class=\"dp-legend\"><i></i>All code 94.8</div><div class=\"dp-row dp-row--axis\"><div class=\"dp-label dp-axis-title\">Line coverage, % (higher is better)</div><div class=\"dp-track dp-axis\"><span class=\"dp-tick\" style=\"left:0.00%\">40.0</span><span class=\"dp-tick\" style=\"left:33.33%\">60.0</span><span class=\"dp-tick\" style=\"left:66.67%\">80.0</span><span class=\"dp-tick\" style=\"left:100.00%\">100.0</span></div><div></div></div><div class=\"dp-row\"><div class=\"dp-label\"><span>Data rules (log.py)</span><span class=\"dp-sub\">109 tests · 173 statements</span></div><div class=\"dp-track\"><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:0.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:33.33%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:66.67%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:100.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-ref\" style=\"left:91.25%\"></span><span class=\"dp-dot\" style=\"left:100.00%\" title=\"Data rules (log.py): 100.0\"></span></div><div class=\"dp-value\">100.0</div></div><div class=\"dp-row\"><div class=\"dp-label\"><span>Storage (db.py)</span><span class=\"dp-sub\">24 tests</span></div><div class=\"dp-track\"><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:0.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:33.33%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:66.67%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:100.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-ref\" style=\"left:91.25%\"></span><span class=\"dp-dot\" style=\"left:100.00%\" title=\"Storage (db.py): 100.0\"></span></div><div class=\"dp-value\">100.0</div></div><div class=\"dp-row\"><div class=\"dp-label\"><span>Reading features</span><span class=\"dp-sub\">19 tests</span></div><div class=\"dp-track\"><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:0.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:33.33%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:66.67%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:100.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-ref\" style=\"left:91.25%\"></span><span class=\"dp-dot\" style=\"left:100.00%\" title=\"Reading features: 100.0\"></span></div><div class=\"dp-value\">100.0</div></div><div class=\"dp-row\"><div class=\"dp-label\"><span>Brand and charts</span><span class=\"dp-sub\">6 tests</span></div><div class=\"dp-track\"><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:0.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:33.33%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:66.67%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:100.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-ref\" style=\"left:91.25%\"></span><span class=\"dp-dot\" style=\"left:100.00%\" title=\"Brand and charts: 100.0\"></span></div><div class=\"dp-value\">100.0</div></div><div class=\"dp-row\"><div class=\"dp-label\"><span>Demo history</span><span class=\"dp-sub\">11 tests, shared with the export</span></div><div class=\"dp-track\"><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:0.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:33.33%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:66.67%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:100.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-ref\" style=\"left:91.25%\"></span><span class=\"dp-dot\" style=\"left:98.37%\" title=\"Demo history: 99.0\"></span></div><div class=\"dp-value\">99.0</div></div><div class=\"dp-row\"><div class=\"dp-label\"><span>Tracker app</span><span class=\"dp-sub\">22 click-through tests</span></div><div class=\"dp-track\"><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:0.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:33.33%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:66.67%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:100.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-ref\" style=\"left:91.25%\"></span><span class=\"dp-dot\" style=\"left:94.52%\" title=\"Tracker app: 96.7\"></span></div><div class=\"dp-value\">96.7</div></div><div class=\"dp-row\"><div class=\"dp-label\"><span>Finish estimate</span><span class=\"dp-sub\">6 tests</span></div><div class=\"dp-track\"><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:0.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:33.33%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:66.67%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:100.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-ref\" style=\"left:91.25%\"></span><span class=\"dp-dot\" style=\"left:91.87%\" title=\"Finish estimate: 95.1\"></span></div><div class=\"dp-value\">95.1</div></div><div class=\"dp-row\"><div class=\"dp-label\"><span>Dashboard app</span><span class=\"dp-sub\">5 click-through tests</span></div><div class=\"dp-track\"><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:0.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:33.33%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:66.67%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:100.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-ref\" style=\"left:91.25%\"></span><span class=\"dp-dot\" style=\"left:91.45%\" title=\"Dashboard app: 94.9\"></span></div><div class=\"dp-value\">94.9</div></div><div class=\"dp-row\"><div class=\"dp-label\"><span>Privacy export</span><span class=\"dp-sub\">11 tests, shared with the demo</span></div><div class=\"dp-track\"><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:0.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:33.33%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:66.67%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:100.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-ref\" style=\"left:91.25%\"></span><span class=\"dp-dot\" style=\"left:90.20%\" title=\"Privacy export: 94.1\"></span></div><div class=\"dp-value\">94.1</div></div><div class=\"dp-row dp-row--hot\"><div class=\"dp-label\"><span>Windows launcher</span><span class=\"dp-sub\">4 tests · 50 statements</span></div><div class=\"dp-track\"><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:0.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:33.33%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:66.67%\"></span><span class=\"dp-grid\" style=\"left:100.00%\"></span><span class=\"dp-ref\" style=\"left:91.25%\"></span><span class=\"dp-dot\" style=\"left:16.67%\" title=\"Windows launcher: 50.0\"></span></div><div class=\"dp-value\">50.0</div></div></div><figcaption>Line coverage per module: the share of its statements that the 206 tests run, on v1.0.0. The launcher&#x27;s untested half starts the server and opens the browser.</figcaption></figure>\n\n<p>Version 1.0.0 works end to end: tracker, export, demo data and dashboard, with ruff and pytest running in CI on every push<sup class=\"cite\"><a href=\"#sources\" title=\"Source: vault note reading-tracker\">[src]</a></sup>. 206 tests pass and cover 94.75% of the code. Line coverage is the share of code statements that the tests actually run. The rules that guard the data are fully covered, and click-through tests drive both apps the way I use them<sup class=\"cite\"><a href=\"#sources\" title=\"Source: vault note reading-tracker\">[src]</a></sup>.</p>\n<p>The gap is the Windows double-click launcher, at 50.0%. The untested half starts the server in the background and opens the browser. The finish-date estimate has no accuracy figure yet: measuring it needs my real history and a backtest, which is the next step<sup class=\"cite\"><a href=\"#sources\" title=\"Source: vault note reading-tracker\">[src]</a></sup>.</p>\n<h2>What I learned</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Friction decides the data.</strong> The tracker is built around one Start and one Stop button, prefilled with the last page. Everything else hides in expanders.</li>\n<li><strong>Privacy rules interact.</strong> Hiding exact times by rounding both ends would have destroyed durations. Publishing the start hour plus the duration keeps pace honest while hiding the clock.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Tools</h2>\n<p>Python, uv, SQLite, pandas, Streamlit, Plotly, pytest, ruff, GitHub Actions, Claude Code.</p>\n<h2>Links</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Code repository: <a href=\"https://github.com/feitandodatascience/reading-tracker\">https://github.com/feitandodatascience/reading-tracker</a></li>\n</ul>",
